# Byte-for-byte checkouts on every platform.
#
# The fixtures under internal/testdata are compressed and compared byte for
# byte, and internal/fse's ExampleCompress asserts an exact input and output
# size. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, so without this a
# Windows checkout rewrites the single LF in e.txt to CRLF — 100003 bytes
# become 100004, the FSE alphabet gains a symbol, and the example fails with a
# one-byte difference that looks like a codec bug.
#
# Disabling text conversion repo-wide is the safe fix: Go sources are LF by
# convention, gofmt emits LF, and nothing here needs CRLF. After adding this to
# an existing Windows clone, run `git add --renormalize .` once.
* -text

# Binary fixtures: don't try to diff them.
*.bin binary
*.data binary
*.gz binary
*.out binary
*.zip binary
